<article class="legal-content">
    <p class="legal-updated">Effective date: November 25, 2026</p>
    <p>These terms describe use of BLife PH, a platform that helps people and participating healthcare facilities share blood requests and donation offers. The verified legal identity and contact details of the platform operator are not configured in this project and should be published before production use.</p>

    <h3>Using an account</h3>
    <p>Provide accurate information, protect your sign-in credentials, and use only accounts you are authorized to access. You are responsible for activity performed through your account. Keep your profile and availability current, and do not impersonate another person or facility.</p>

    <h3>Blood requests and donation offers</h3>
    <p>Post only information you are authorized to share. If you publish on behalf of a patient or another person, obtain their permission and avoid identifying or sensitive medical details. Requests and offers reflect user-submitted information; BLife PH does not verify that blood is needed, that a donor is eligible or available, or that a facility has inventory. Update or close posts when circumstances change.</p>
    <p>Use the platform's messaging and response features respectfully. Do not treat a response or offer as a confirmed appointment, medical clearance, or guarantee of donation.</p>

    <h3>Clinics and blood banks</h3>
    <p>Facility accounts are created by administrators, not through public clinic registration. Authorized facility staff must use the account only for their institution, keep facility details accurate, protect temporary credentials, and submit requests, offers, and events on behalf of others only with appropriate permission.</p>

    <h3>Prohibited activity</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Fraud, impersonation, harassment, threats, spam, or deceptive requests and offers.</li>
        <li>Posting another person's private contact, location, patient record, test result, or other sensitive information without authority.</li>
        <li>Using the platform to sell blood, make unsupported medical claims, bypass clinical screening, or interfere with authorized healthcare services.</li>
        <li>Attempting to access accounts, posts, messages, or facility information without permission, or disrupting the platform.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Medical and emergency disclaimer</h3>
    <p>BLife PH is a communication and discovery platform. It does not collect, screen, store, transport, distribute, or transfuse blood; provide medical advice; assess donor eligibility or compatibility; confirm blood inventory; or coordinate emergency care. Qualified healthcare professionals and authorized facilities must make all clinical decisions. For emergencies, contact local emergency services or a healthcare facility directly.</p>

    <h3>Platform limitations and content</h3>
    <p>Posts, locations, and availability are supplied by users and may be incomplete, inaccurate, or out of date. Map markers are approximate and are not a navigation or emergency service. BLife PH does not guarantee that a post will receive a response, that a match will be found, or that the service will be continuously available. The platform may moderate, restrict, or remove content or accounts when needed to protect users or operate the service.</p>
    <p>Third-party services, including OpenStreetMap map tiles and configured email delivery, are subject to their own terms and policies. Users must not misuse those services through BLife PH.</p>

    <h3>Account changes and deletion requests</h3>
    <p>You may deactivate your account or request account deletion through Settings &amp; Privacy. A deletion request is not an immediate deletion command. The platform operator must review the request and consider related conversations, requests, safety records, and applicable retention requirements before taking action.</p>

    <h3>Changes and contact</h3>
    <p>These terms may be updated as platform features or practices change. The effective date above identifies the current version. A verified contact address for the platform operator is not currently configured; contact the site administrator through the support channel provided to you.</p>
</article>
